set_option doc.verso.module true

/-!
# Week 1

In this introductory week, you will learn the meaning of, and be able to identify, hypotheses,
goals, and targets in Lean proofs.

Interrogate the InfoView window to examine the goals 

You will create Lean proofs using the {tactic}`rw` tactic for rewriting a target using a hypothesis
or lemma, either forwards or backwards:

You will create equational-style Lean proofs using the {tactic}`calc` tactic.

You will introduce new hypotheses into the context using the {tactic}`have` tactic.

Moreover, you will learn how to interact with git and GitHub Codespaces so that you can:

* create a fork of the course repository in GitHub;
* create a Codespaces container in which you will run Lean;
* edit files within your Codespaces container;
* stage and commit changes to your Lean files within the container;
* sync the Codespace changes to your fork of the repository;
* sync your fork with the course repository
-/
